<!-- SCE Forge conformance: Zenoh linkstate-peer routing — a single
     `link_weights` element (one edge weight).

     Mirrors the per-element write/read inside zenoh
     `zenoh/src/net/codec/linkstate.rs:74-79` / `:121-131`:

         for w in link_weights.iter() { codec.write(writer, w)?; }   // &u16
         ...
         let w: u16 = codec.read(reader)?;

     IMPORTANT — the weight is VLE-encoded, NOT a fixed 2-byte int:
     `codec.write(w)` (w: &u16) resolves WCodec<&u16> -> WCodec<u16> ->
     `self.write(writer, x as u64)` (commons/zenoh-codec/src/core/
     zint.rs:212-214 -> :181-183) = the base-128 VLE u64 path. Decode is
     the mirror (`:192-194` reads a VLE u64, casts to u16). So a weight
     value in 0..=127 is one wire byte, 128..=16383 two bytes, etc. This
     is DISTINCT from the fixed little-endian 2-byte `batch_size`
     (init_body/join) — those use `_z_uint16_encode`; link_weights ride
     the wider VLE path. Like `linkstate_link` wraps a bare VLE u64, this
     wraps a bare VLE u64 so it can be a `<sce:repeat>` element type
     (SCE repeats codec aliases, not scalars).

     THE FIELD IS DECLARED AT THE WIRE'S WIDTH, NOT THE VALUE'S — the two
     are different facts and this file used to collapse them (R311y880).
     `uint16` made SCE emit `cursor.read_vle_u16()`, which REFUSES both a
     value past `u16::MAX` and any encoding longer than 3 bytes. Upstream
     refuses neither: the mirror at `:192-194` is the plain `Zenoh080`
     whose `uint_impl!(u16)` derive is `let x: u64 = self.read(reader)?;
     Ok(x as $uint)` — it reads the full ZInt and TRUNCATES. The codec
     that refuses an out-of-range zint is `Zenoh080Bounded<u16>`, which
     this field does not select. So a refusing read here did not make wz
     stricter, it made wz DROP a topology advertisement that every
     conforming peer folds into its routing table — and, because a
     too-narrow read stops mid-varint, leave the cursor inside the field.
     The VALUE width is applied once, by name, at the consumer boundary:
     `wz_codecs::wire_const::linkstate_weight_from_wire`.

     Wire shape:
       byte 0+ : weight  (VLE ZInt, an edge weight truncated to u16 by
                          every reader; default 100 when the peer omits
                          the WGT block — see linkstate.rs
                          LinkEdgeWeight::DEFAULT_LINK_WEIGHT).

     Composition: B1-alpha VLE only. No new primitive surface. -->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       sce:kind="codec" sce:default-endian="big" name="linkstate_weight">
  <datamodel>
    <sce:field id="weight" sce:type="uint64" sce:byte="0" sce:bit-size="vle"/>
  </datamodel>
</scxml>
